            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jillian"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this again for lunch today and it was delicious! I added a little garlic powder and increased the mayo. I actually use lite mayo and finely chopped red onion. This is good with or without the dill pickle. Serve it on toast or with a garden salad inside a hollowed out tomato or red pepper and it's a lite lunch that's attractive and good for you!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Asya Su"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made mine with red onion and to save time on chopping and mixing the ingredients, I just dumped everything in a food processor and blended it for like 10secs. It came out perfect! Reminds me of the tuna salad you get at bagel places or the kind you use for a tuna melt.",
            "datePublished": "2021-02-24T20:52:04.680Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "cbexpress"
            },
            "reviewBody": "On a calorie restricted diet the Hubby and I have to find high protein - low calorie meal options. I made this (skipping the mayo) used spicy brown mustard - served rolled in Romaine Lettuce leaves topped with fresh garden tomato slices. TASTY!!",
            "datePublished": "2017-09-19T15:50:22.040Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Beebs3179"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I'm allergic to eggs, therefore I can't use mayonnaise. I substituted salad dressing. I use either catalina , zesty Italian or roasted garlic vinaigrette. It comes out very well, and if you're not crazy about dill pickle relish try sweet pickle relish. It puts a different zing to the salad.",
            "datePublished": "2020-10-01T21:36:53.040Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "maggiemai"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It was all right, however I had to brighten it up a bit by adding a bit of BBQ sauce- yes, you heard me right, BBQ sauce- and added some crunch with chopped up pickles in place of the relish; I'm not going to lie, but I had to splurge and add some more mayo as well to take away from it's dryness. Served mine on a whole wheat pita that was browned on both sides under the broiler.",
            "datePublished": "2012-06-29T12:48:22.667Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "vbm9210"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love this recipe but made a few changes. In addition to the recipe, I use 1/8 cup of mayo, add 1/2 tsp dill, 1/2-1 cup grapes (cut in half), a sprinkle of salt and pepper, and a 1/8 cup spicy almonds (homemade). This recipe is a little dry so you definitely have to up the mayo and adding the spices makes it very flavorful. I use the same recipe for chicken salad and they are so tasty!",
            "datePublished": "2015-06-22T19:02:11.937Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Rachella"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I really liked this tuna salad recipe but I added twice the amount of mayonnaise because it makes the salad not so dry but a nice, creamy mix. Also, add more sweet relish and Dijon mustard to truly make it taste zesty.",
            "datePublished": "2019-09-12T20:23:10.617Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "EmWillFish"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I really liked this recipe! But after making it, I thought that I'd put my own spin on things by adding noodles. I used the same ingredients (except I almost tripled them) added a little (about 1 tbs) of lemon juice, vinegar, canola oil, and onion powder, sprinkled cheese on top, and then added the mixture to spiral noodles. I chilled in the fridge for about two hours. It was excellent!",
            "datePublished": "2009-07-22T13:35:15.020Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lucieana"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used a red onion, added more mayo (light), powdered garlic, and paprika. I usually find tuna sandwiches to be very bland, this one was already better even without my tweaking. I based my tweaking on some of the reviews and now it's wonderful.",
            "datePublished": "2016-02-27T13:18:04.257Z"
          },
          {
